From: Leo Yan <leo.yan@arm.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 03:34:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] coresight: perf: Retrieve path and source from event data

commit f37bc31447c0ddafedb25e3c4a4f4e2284034247 upstream.

[ Backport: 6.1 has no struct coresight_path. coresight_get_source() is new here and takes the list_head path. ]
[ Backport: 6.1 has no coresight_is_device_source(). Check CORESIGHT_DEV_TYPE_SOURCE directly. ]
[ Backport: 6.1 has no AUX pause/resume. Drop etm_event_get_ctxt_path(), the pause/resume changes and the READ_ONCE()/WRITE_ONCE() accessors. ]
[ Backport: 6.1 stops the tracer with source_ops()->disable(), not coresight_disable_source(). Keep that call, on the source from the path. ]

ETM perf callbacks currently use the per-CPU csdev_src pointer, which
can race with updates during device registration and unregistration.

The AUX setup already builds and stores the path in the event data.
Use this path to retrieve the source instead of csdev_src to avoid
the race.

Export coresight_get_source() and add etm_event_get_ctxt_path() to
retrieve the context's path and its source with READ_ONCE() /
WRITE_ONCE() accessors. Give the comments to explain why this
approach is safe when pause or resume callbacks preempt the disable
callback (e.g. via NMI).

